        <H1>
          Slider vs SliderW
        </H1>

        <Markdown>
          <![CDATA[
These tests show what **SliderW** can do that **Slider** can't.
`SliderNative.tsx` accepts props that the hand-written renderer never forwards.
`wrapComponent` forwards everything automatically, so these "just work."

## Tracing

Open the inspector (gear icon) and compare what happens when you move each slider. **Slider** produces only handler execution events (`handler:start`, `state:changes`, `handler:complete`) — it tells you *code ran*. **SliderW** also produces semantic behavioral events like `value:change SliderW "60"` and `focus:change` — it tells you *what the user did*. These are the events that [trace-tools](https://github.com/xmlui-org/trace-tools) needs to generate Playwright test steps and compare traces across runs. The hand-written renderer is invisible to the trace system; `wrapComponent` makes every wrapped component traceable.
]]>
        </Markdown>

